{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And Moses brought their case.</b> The halakhah was hidden from him, and here he was punished for having taken the crown to say ״וְהַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר יִקְשֶׁה מִכֶּם תַּקְרִבוּן אֵלַי״ (Deuteronomy 1). Another interpretation: this passage was fit to be written by Moses, but the daughters of Tzelofchad merited and it was written through them (Bava Batra 119a; Sanhedrin 8a)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:59.280826070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}